#NEXUS

[ müller2018a_fig2: Sauropodomorph time tree, read with a listing of the grey line segments from the pixels. Sauropodomorpha and Unaysauridae (red arrows), Plateosauria and Massopoda (printed beside the stems entering their nodes) and Massospondylidae (beside its stem) are kept as internal labels. Polytomies: Saturnalia, Panphagia, Chromogisaurus and Pampadromaeus; and Pantydraco, Thecodontosaurus and Arcusaurus (the Thecodontosaurus line runs from the node's parent across the node's vertical and is read as its stem with Thecodontosaurus a child, as in earlier batches). 31 tips, 2 polytomies (4, 3 children); 5 printed clade names kept as internal node labels. Sample 5 case (census 2, seed 20261215). Topology transcribed from the figure image and checked node by node; topology only. ]

